}^{2}-4{x}^{2}=36$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-4(0)^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,2)$ and $(0,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Hyperbola and a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cdf9991-54c0-5907-b4c4-386c77f27b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cdf9991-54c0-5907-b4c4-386c77f27b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283902} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4c7cc2-2d02-5c8a-a77e-2125403b00b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc988383-1e89-5565-9753-3d079cedb0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc988383-1e89-5565-9753-3d079cedb0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283904} :answer-field/id #uuid "84db0e4a-cac2-5576-81dd-9da53bef1cd8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51629e1f-11aa-5026-a109-70d1b9705db2" :question/math-academy-id "q-277805" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=8$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Hyperbola and a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "730c0f83-755b-5070-89cf-87b3254ec271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264782} {:answer/id #uuid "bae71417-2834-58a6-943c-7f0ad123769b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "730c0f83-755b-5070-89cf-87b3254ec271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264782} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1651f2-d37a-54c2-9114-eef3e43f2e83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be5a155-b40c-5e7a-b681-207b7fa85dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3be5a155-b40c-5e7a-b681-207b7fa85dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264785} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edf9491-9b0f-5433-9cc4-2aaf28bc63a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bea3b57-2a79-53a0-be43-d2e4d30fedc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-278375" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1$ intersects the line $y=-x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84fae736-399a-5371-9e9d-8484ee13deaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087145} {:answer/id #uuid "1c68ae03-2ab0-5e0d-ae49-205b0b2138ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no $y$-intercepts" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087146} {:answer/id #uuid "29c705fe-2df4-5cac-ab5d-741d0bb0c632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, ± 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087147} {:answer/id #uuid "5624da29-141f-5a43-b364-63297517048a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087148} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb6e9bb-46d9-5c52-bc31-4026991e8d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, ± 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c68ae03-2ab0-5e0d-ae49-205b0b2138ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no $y$-intercepts" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087146} :answer-field/id #uuid "321f0aca-1d7c-55e9-ac65-c704df881437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087144}] :question/id #uuid "73a6a21a-1a66-5641-b8d4-54583c604a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-84041" :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $((x - 2)^{2})/(5) - ((y + 4)^{2})/(16) = 1$."}]}
